PATCH 488: the steering / obstacle-avoidance driver aea8 and its sibling countdown af0b.

aea8 (asm 0xaea8-0xaf0a, di = the object's NEAR offset) searches for a collision-free heading every 4th
tick: from the commanded azimuth word[di+0x26] it tries up to 15 offsets word[DGROUP:0x97aa+idx],
projecting each with 03a9(angle,0x20) into dword[0x9962]/[0x9966] and asking af1c (patch 487).  af1c's
CF=0 means CLEAR and BREAKS the search (`jae 0xaef0`); the chosen heading is committed as word[di+0x47] =
word[di+0x26] + word[DGROUP:0x97ba+idx].  Ghidra read both offset tables 4 bytes wide, stored 03a9's dx
INPUT (the constant 0x20) where the asm stores its DX OUTPUT, and replaced af1c's CF with the bogus
`(long)iVar5 << 2 < 0` -- so the search never terminated early and always committed the last candidate.
af0b (asm 0xaf0b-0xaf1b) is the same countdown without the search; Ghidra deref'd di as a host pointer
(INDIA1's self-play SEGV'd there) and tested the WORD flag [di+0x40] 32 bits wide.
